> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think posting the exact same thing in three different threads is a bit excessive. I follow different forums instead of individual threads so it clogs up my subscription list, and two of the threads are even in the same subforum so it's not like anyone would miss only one of those.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So noted, my apologies, I was posting from my mobile to my recent post thread.<br /> In case they are only following one thread, I also would not like them to miss it.<br /> Is there a way to combine them, or should they be combined?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T05:53:17-08:00","id":1353326,"title":"","content":"You could post a link in two of them to the one you want to keep. Anyone following them will see which thread will be updated in the future. You could also ask a mod to close the other threads after that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T09:16:28-08:00","id":1353371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Graylion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1332504-cod-vtr-to-storypath?p=1353279#post1353279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using the Storypath Rules to run Vampire the Requiem.<br /> <br /> Best regards</div> </div> </div> </div>So are the storypath rules better suited to running VtR?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T11:47:11-08:00","id":1353393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1332504-cod-vtr-to-storypath?p=1353371#post1353371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So are the storypath rules better suited to running VtR?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In my experience VTR/COD become a race for who has the biggest bonus and largest handfuls of dice.<br /> <br /> Storypath adds some mundane modifier balances, enhancements, and complications into the mix while adding Scale rules which consider when when two sides are matched or unmatched.<br /> <br /> For example a Giant may be Scale 3 against a mortal who is Scale 0, this applied give the Giant automatic sucesses which really highlight and speed the system.<br /> Also I have seen many one shots kills of important enemies that went way to quick. Storypath implements an injury / critial injury based on stunts (additional successes). 5 extra succcesses in COD/VTR would amount to 5 damage, where as this in Storypath would be one injurt and a second critical injury for a total of two damage on a much smaller health charts.<br /> <br /> I think they flattened the weapons and armor a bit to fit this damage and health, but Im adding a few custom items to smooth it out for myself.<br /> <br /> Just a couople of items off the top of my head.<br /> <br /> Your milage may vary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T12:52:15-08:00","id":1353404,"title":"","content":"Those do sound like large benefits, but the amounts of &quot;stuff&quot; for each gameline (Disciplines, Devotions, etc... for vampires) does seem quite magic. Guess I'll see how far you end up taking it. ^^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T13:05:49-08:00","id":1353408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Unahim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1332504-cod-vtr-to-storypath?p=1353404#post1353404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those do sound like large benefits, but the amounts of &quot;stuff&quot; for each gameline (Disciplines, Devotions, etc... for vampires) does seem quite magic. Guess I'll see how far you end up taking it. ^^</div> </div> </div> </div>Ya it is a large undertaking. I am starting with Vampire the Requiem and once I have the bones of one COD line done it will be easier with each additional line. The blood sorcery of VTR will help me with the Mage part. I invision Mage as being the hardest of them. <br /> <br /> The home page is <a href=\"https://www.worldanvil.com/w/creation\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> The Landing Page is <a href=\"https://www.worldanvil.com/w/creation/a/landing\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> with a lot of my work so far.<br /> <br /> The current Campaign Introduction is <a href=\"https://www.worldanvil.com/w/creation/a/shadow-war-introduction-article-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> I am always looking for feedback.<br /> <br /> Best regards","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T16:49:16-08:00","id":1353450,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25095_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25095\" data-vbnamecard=\"25095\">Graylion</a> so you\u2019re keeping the setting, just changing the rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T18:13:23-08:00","id":1353463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1332504-cod-vtr-to-storypath?p=1353450#post1353450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25095_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25095\" data-vbnamecard=\"25095\">Graylion</a> so you\u2019re keeping the setting, just changing the rules?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, but my setting is a fantasy darkages world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-07T19:38:25-08:00","id":1353473,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25095_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25095\" data-vbnamecard=\"25095\">Graylion</a> with vampires? That\u2019s pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T11:09:01-08:00","id":1356127,"title":"","content":"Here are my first couple of Vampire Discipline converted to a Storypath format, very rough draft but welcoming your feedback ...<br /> <br /> <u><b>VIGOR</b></u><br /> <br /> While all Kindred possess the power to bolster their might in short bursts, Vigor allows some vampires to kick like a freight train or rend steel with their bare hands. The Beast tunes every bone, tendon and muscle fiber to its highest performance , allowing the night\u2019s most fearsome predator to strut through the jungle of his choosing without fear of lesser, weaker creatures.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Constant</u></b><br /> Action: None<br /> Cost: None<br /> Duration: Contant<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>POTENCE</b> (Constant)<br /> You are considered to have Scale 1: Might (Enhancement +2) for all things relating to strength, might, close combat, pushing, pulling, lifting.<br /> <br /> <b>POWERFUL LEAP</b> (Constant)<br /> The power in your character\u2019s legs propels her to impossible heights and distances. She is also immune from falling damage from any vertical distance she can jump. Your character can leap over any vertical barrier that is no more than Close range (3m) above her without rolling dice. The jumping distances presented on the chart are averages not requiring a Athletics + Might roll.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Active</u></b><br /> Action: Reflexive<br /> Cost: 1 Vitae<br /> Duration: 1 turn<br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> <br /> <br /> By spending Vitae a vampire can energize her dead muscles, giving her a brief but substantial burst of strength. For each point of Vitae spent choose one effect from the following list. A vampire may spend additional Vitae to invoke multiple effects simultaneously, but no effect of Vigor may be used more than once per turn. The vampire receives the benefit of Dramatic Scale when inflicting damage through sheer<br /> Might.<br /> <br /> <b>STRENGTH OF THE BEAST</b> (Active)<br /> Gain Enhancement from Scale on Close Combat attacks using Might while active. This puts enormous strain on weapons, especially those not intended for heavy hitting. Improvised weapons are easily damaged or broken. This rating is added to you Potence rating to determine your enhancement and scale.<br /> <br /> <b>DEAD LIFTER</b> (Active)<br /> Gain Enhancement from Scale on Athletics using Might while active. Lift and hurl objects normally far too unwieldy to use as weapons, such as boulders, cars, and other people. Any object she can lift, can be used as an improvised melee or throwing weapon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Note on Scale</b><br /> Scale from the same category does not stack, the greater Scale is used. Scale tops out at Scale 5 for most characters. Scale beyond 5 is reserved for Epic entities of an otherworldy nature and possible Elder Kindred.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Vigor</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Enh</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Scale</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Long Jump</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">High Jump</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Contant 1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+2e</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Short 5m</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Close 3m</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Active 1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+3e</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Short 10m</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Short 5m</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Active 2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+4e</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Short 15m</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Short 8m</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Active 3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+5e</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Short 30m</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Short 15m</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Active 4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+6e</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Medium 60m</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Short 30m</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Active 5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+7e</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Long 120m</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Medium 60m</td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-20T11:14:08-08:00","id":1356130,"title":"","content":"<u><b>CELERITY</b></u><br /> <br /> Unleashing her Beast, a vampire can cross vast distances in<br /> the blink of an eye, catch a thrown punch before her attacker has even moved a muscle, or snatch a gun barrel away from a man\u2019s temple before he can pull the trigger. Celerity makes a vampire so fast that it\u2019s as if she never has to move at all.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Constant</u></b><br /> Action: None <br /> Cost: None <br /> Duration: Contant <br /> Dice Pool: None<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>SWIFT</b> (Constant) <br /> You are considered to have Scale 1: Speed (Enhancement +2) to outrace others on foot and all things relating to speed.<br /> <br /> <b>HARD TO HIT</b><br /> Scale 1: Speed (Enhancement +1 Static) to Defense<br /> <br /> <br /> <b><u>Active</u></b> <br /> Action: Reflexive <br /> Cost: 1 Vitae <br /> Duration: 1 turn <br /> Dice Pool: None <br /> <br /> <br /> By spending Vitae Celerity allows for bursts of speed<br /> faster than the eye can perceive. For each point of Vitae spent choose one effect from the following list. A vampire may spend additional Vitae to invoke multiple effects simultaneously, but no effect of Celerity may be used more than once per turn.<br /> <br /> <b>BURST</b><br /> Multiply her speed by her dots in Celerity plus one. Moving in this way is sudden, jarring, the vampire appears to shift from point to point without crossing the space in-between. She may use this to briefly avoid detection or launch surprise attacks.<br /> <br /> The moment the whistle blows, your character is already crossing the finish line. She sprints in a blur, keeping pace with and outstripping swift vehicles and animals. <br /> <br /> <b>FIRST</b> <br /> Immediately move to the head of the Initiative queue. This boost in Initiative lasts only one turn, after which all combatants return to acting in their rolled order. When multiple characters attempt this a Clash of Will wills determine the order of action.<br /> <br /> <b>SEIZE THE MOMENT</b> <br /> Your character anticipates movement around herself, reacting well before others. Your character reacts so quickly she can interrupt others\u2019 actions, seizing focus before another character \u2014 friend or foe. This does not adjust the Initiative Roster.<br /> <br /> The decision to interrupt is made after another character\u2019s action is declared, but before it actually occurs (before dice are rolled). Once interrupted, the other character must continue his declared action, if it\u2019s still possible. If the action is no longer possible, he takes no action. Alternatively, that character\u2019s player may declare his action a Botch and gain 3 Momentum.<br /> <br /> Celerity may not be able to interupt actions of which the character was unaware, depending on the Storyguides detemination. Finally, using Celerity in this way is taxing; a vampire may only interrupt as many actions in a scene as she has dots in Celerity. When multiple characters attempt this a Clash of Will wills determine the order of action.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Interrupt the action of another character with a brief action of<br /> her own. This could be an attack, making it possible to disable an opponent in mid-action. It may be movement, avoiding harm by shifting out of reach. Or it could be any other instant action, like activating a Discipline or dodging. However, the vampire is still limited to one instant action. She cannot use Celerity to make two attacks, or an attack followed by another instant action. Likewise she cannot move further in a single turn than her Speed would allow. <br /> <br /> <b>DODGE BALL</b> <br /> Your character sees the hit coming and prepares, even if it isn\u2019t her turn to act. When someone targets your character with an attack, before dice are rolled, she can automatically increase her Defense. She may do this once per round.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Note on Scale</b> <br /> Scale from the same category does not stack, the greater Scale is used. Scale tops out at Scale 5 for most characters. Scale beyond 5 is reserved for Epic entities of an otherworldy nature and possible Elder Kindred.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Celerity</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Enh</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Scale</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Defense Static</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Speed</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Human</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+0e</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">0</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+0e</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Short 10m</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Contant 1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+2e</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+1e</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Short 30m</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Active 1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+3e</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+2e</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Medium 60m</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Active 2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+4e</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+2e</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Long 120m</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Active 3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+5e</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+3e</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Long 250m</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Active 4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+6e</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+3e</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Long 500m</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\">Active 5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+7e</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">+4e</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\">Long 1000m</td> </tr> </table></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"> <hr /><b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Roleplaying</span> not <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Rollplaying</span> or <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Ruleplaying</span></span></b></div> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><u><b>Current</b> <b>Focus</b></u><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Storypath &amp; Storypath to Run CoD, VtR, WtF, MtA</span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\"><b>Dungeons &amp; Dragons 5th Edition</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25095-graylion","name":"Graylion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"368"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}